Package: isolatr
Title: Simulate and Evaluate Isolation Testing Strategies for Infectious Diseases
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kylie", "Ainslie", , "kylie.ainslie@unimelb.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("David", "Price", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0076-3123")),
    person("Joshua", "Ross", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Provides tools for simulating infectious disease transmission dynamics
    during isolation/quarantine and evaluating the effectiveness of different testing
    strategies. The package implements a stochastic simulation model that accounts for
    household structure, vaccination status, isolation timing, and various
    Test-Trace-Isolate-Quarantine (TTIQ) scenarios. While defaults are calibrated to
    COVID-19, all epidemiological parameters are configurable for other diseases.
    It enables users to compare testing schedules and quantify their impact on
    reducing onwards transmission from isolated individuals.
